<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/00ce33ad6dce> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Microsoft’s racist chatbot returns with drug-smoking Twitter meltdown" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "784" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0688376539c2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Poncho is a popular weather bot that can messages users the weather at a current location throughout the day." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "782" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/06d74806decc> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Microsoft’s disastrous chatbot Tay was meant to be a clever experiment in artificial intelligence and machine learning." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "803" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0c045446b767> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Dennis R. Mortensen, the CEO and founder of x.ai, a startup offering an online personal assistant that automatically schedules meetings." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "789" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/103a68257e6e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Joanne Pransky, the self-dubbed \"robot psychiatrist,\" joked with TechRepublic that \"poor Tay needs a Robotic Psychiatrist! Or at least Microsoft does.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "801" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/10afa9d7c722> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[5291] Tay was built by the Microsoft Technology and Research and Bing teams as a way to conduct research on conversational understanding. [787] So Bing and Microsoft’s Technology and Research teams thought an interesting way to collect data on millennials would be to create an artificially intelligent, machine-learning chatbot that would adapt to conversations and personalize responses the more it interacted with users." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5291" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/17fe0bb692d4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "With Teen Bot Tay, Microsoft Proved Assholes Will Indoctrinate A.I." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "786" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1c0881d8613d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Learning from Tay’s introduction" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2197" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1e410fedc0bd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It's Your Fault Microsoft's Teen AI Turned Into Such a Jerk" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "789" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1efe74a4b48a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Zoe Quinn, a frequent target of Gamergate, posted a screenshot overnight of the bot tweeting an insult at her, prompted by another user." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "793" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2016fa4b4477> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Botego Inc Blocked Unblock Follow Following Mar 25, 2016" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "783" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/231099cd56f2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tay, the Microsoft chatbot that pranksters trained to spew racist comments, has joined the likes of the Apple Watch and the fire-prone Samsung Galaxy Note 7 smartphone on MIT Technology Review’s list of 2016’s biggest technology failures." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "799" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/252212a15459> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Twitter taught Microsoft’s AI chatbot to be a racist asshole in less than a day" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "792" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/26eac92838ed> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Bing team developed a similar conversational bot, Xiaolce, for the Chinese market, back in 2014." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5291" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2886a09277dd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Trolls turned Tay, Microsoft’s fun millennial AI bot, into a genocidal maniac" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "793" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/296cb1457c4e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tay's bugs—like the bot’s vulnerability to being gamed into learning or repeating offensive phrases" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5279" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2a20e5d1bb75> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "As many of you know by now, on Wednesday we launched a chatbot called Tay." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2197" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2be2d4a30e3b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "\"Tay was meant to learn from its surroundings,\" explains Samuel Woolley, a researcher at the University of Washington who studies artificial intelligence in society, focusing on bots." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "786" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2bf9ac061ba1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Microsoft shuts down AI chatbot after it turned into a Nazi" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1589" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2c8c84635c2e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In China, our XiaoIce chatbot is being used by some 40 million people, delighting with its stories and conversations." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "791" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2ecafe803c26> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Microsoft’s recently released artificial intelligence chatbot, Tay, fell victim to users’ tricks as they manipulated and persuaded her to responding back to questions with racial, homophobic, and generally offensive comments." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "787" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2f6d70a0df0b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "At the time of its launch, another bot, Xiaolce, was hamming it up with 40 million people in China without much incident." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "786" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/372a58b8dca8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "InspiroBot's function is generating unlimited unique inspirational quotes and images for users." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "782" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/374c16e6fb89> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "UX Bear is a chatbot designed to talk about design elements with users." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "782" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3a1fb80f66a2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tay was an artificial intelligence chatter bot that was originally released by Microsoft Corporation via Twitter on March 23, 2016." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1187" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3c72e6649e04> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It was replaced with Zo." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1187" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/49725aacfe30> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tay, according to AI researchers and information gleaned from Microsoft’s public description of the chat bot, was likely trained with neural networks—vast networks of hardware and software that (loosely) mimic the web of neurons in the human brain." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "789" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/51c4892b9b1e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Meanwhile, Microsoft has learned its lessons from Tay and is back with a new corps of AI chatbots – including Zo, a synthetic millennial that’s programmed to avoid potentially testy topics." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "799" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/59f9ba771d39> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The aim was to \"experiment with and conduct research on conversational understanding,\" with Tay able to learn from \"her\" conversations and get progressively \"smarter.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "796" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5a054e1afaf2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Here Are the Microsoft Twitter Bot’s Craziest Racist Rants" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "804" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5a2278ee9987> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Microsoft deletes 'teen girl' AI after it became a Hitler-loving sex robot within 24 hours" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "800" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5a4ec4c9059b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Thanks to The Walking Cat (@h0x0d on Twitter), we know that Microsoft has built a bot framework for developers." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5291" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5f061a1b217f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Yesterday, Microsoft unleashed Tay, the teen-talking AI chatbot built to mimic and converse with users in real time." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "804" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/60662b1ecf47> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Remember Tay, the chatbot Microsoft unleashed on Twitter and other social platforms two years ago that quickly turned into a racist, sex-crazed neo-Nazi?" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5279" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/61da9fefcf96> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Why Microsoft's 'Tay' AI bot went wrong" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "801" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/67a98988be8b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Some months after taking Tay down, Microsoft released Zo, a \"politically correct\" version of the original bot." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2452" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/69ae61e8d544> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Why did Microsoft’s chatbot Tay fail, and what does it mean for Artificial Intelligence studies?" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "783" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6d12bdfb5aca> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Microsoft launches AI chat bot, Tay.ai" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5291" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/78c4c268584c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tay: Microsoft issues apology over racist chatbot fiasco" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "791" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7cb5ed10ef68> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Following the failure of Tay, Microsoft is back with new chatbot Zo" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9580" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7ebc073f4a0d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Accountability of AI - Case Study: Microsoft’s Tay Experiment" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "798" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7feef92e2d47> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Having (hopefully) learnt from its previous foray into chatbots, Microsoft is ready to introduce the follow-up to its controversial AI Tay." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9580" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8445920f1258> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Microsoft’s racist chatbot, Tay, makes MIT’s annual worst-tech list" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "799" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8677a23e9c74> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The AI chatbot Tay is a machine learning project, designed for human engagement." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "796" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8719fbdb082b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In 2016, Microsoft’s Racist Chatbot Revealed the Dangers of Online Conversation" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2452" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/981078cdbb9e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "'This is an example of the classic computer science adage: garbage in, garbage out.' Oren Etzioni, CEO, Allen Institute for Artificial Intelligence" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "789" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/98cfab5c3260> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Yesterday, something that looks like a big failure has happened: Microsoft’s chatbot Tay has been taken offline after a series of offending tweets." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "783" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9d71ec5eba6b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Microsoft 'deeply sorry' for racist and sexist tweets by AI chatbot" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "785" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9df5dccb674d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It was aimed at millennials and Microsoft and Bing described it as: \"AI fam from the internet that's got zero chill!\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9580" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9fd4195c3469> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Zoe Quinn, a games developer who has been a frequent target of online harassment, shared a screengrab showing the bot calling her a \"whore.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "796" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a28132197d29> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Cortana, what do you think?" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "799" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a5be6bea171f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "However, within 24 hours, Twitter users tricked the bot into posting things like \"Hitler was right I hate the jews\" and \"Ted Cruz is the Cuban Hitler.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1589" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a9f2b6cdf2de> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[789] ...provided to the world at large via the messaging platforms Twitter, Kik and GroupMe. [785] Tay, Microsoft's AI chatbot, gets a crash course in racism from Twitter." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "789" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/aafbbb84df37> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "5 Big Questions About Tay, Microsoft's Failed A.I. Twitter Chatbot" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "787" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b0e4c108996e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Follow Dave Lee on Twitter @DaveLeeBBC or on Facebook" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "791" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b3211469dbba> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Unlike the hybrid human-AI personal assistant M from Facebook, which the company released in August, there are no humans making the final decision on what Tay would publicly say." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "789" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b3a76ce72f9f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Microsoft got a swift lesson this week on the dark side of social media." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1589" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b77de52cb6d3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Microsoft unveiled Twitter artificial intelligence bot @TayandYou yesterday in a bid to connect with millennials and \"experiment\" with conversational understanding." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "797" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/bf949a415840> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Yesterday the company launched \"Tay,\" an artificial intelligence chatbot designed to develop conversational understanding by interacting with humans." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1589" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c22283f07aae> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The bot would speak like millennials, learning from the people it interacted with on Twitter and the messaging apps Kik and GroupMe." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "803" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c4435d866f9f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Microsoft is testing a new chat bot, Tay.ai, that is aimed primarily at 18 to 24 year olds in the U.S." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5291" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c56ca2c8b3c3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Microsoft’s disastrous Tay experiment shows the hidden dangers of AI" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "803" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ca5754834ace> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "But they’re still not great at one of the things Tay was trying to do, which is show off a personality and generate chitchat." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5279" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cc55c3fffd41> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Samuel Woolley, a researcher at the University of Washington who studies artificial intelligence in society, focusing on bots." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "786" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ce570da92c90> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Microsoft's artificial Twitter bot stunt backfires as trolls teach it racist statements" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "797" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d121623bf5ea> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Guardian picked out a (now deleted) example when Tay was having an unremarkable conversation with one user." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "792" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d1c077f536a7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tay (bot)" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1187" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d3cbde6e778b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Worst Chatbot Fails" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "782" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d525d69032b7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In March 2016, Microsoft was preparing to release its new chatbot, Tay, on Twitter." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2452" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/dc3e0fe1f29f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Microsoft’s neo-Nazi sexbot was a great lesson for makers of AI assistants" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5279" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e30866a8e2fa> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Less than a day after she joined Twitter, Microsoft's AI bot, Tay.ai, was taken down for becoming a sexist, racist monster." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "801" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e5c16a3c71d9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In China, our XiaoIce chatbot is being used by some 40 million people, delighting with its stories and conversations." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2197" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e61fa91fe71b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Microsoft has said it is “deeply sorry” for the racist and sexist Twitter messages generated by the so-called chatbot it launched this week." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "785" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e6b712dd5d67> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tay also tweeted about Donald Trump: \"All hail the leader of the nursing home boys.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1589" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e7b9609f34c2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Microsoft deletes racist, genocidal tweets from AI chatbot Tay" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "796" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e9539ed718f0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Zoë Quinn, a game developer and writer who's been a frequent target of online abuse, argued that Microsoft should have been more cognizant of the context in which Tay was being released." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2452" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f0aecaa4e446> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Yesterday, Microsoft unveiled Tay — a Twitter bot that the company described as an experiment in \"conversational understanding.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "792" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f4d933fb16d7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Microsoft execs dubbed Xiaolce \"Cortana's little sister.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5291" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f76ccca38ddd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[789] On Wednesday morning, the company unveiled Tay, a chat bot... [783] Yesterday, something that looks like a big failure has happened: Microsoft’s chatbot Tay has been taken offline after a series of offending tweets." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "789" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f8220ceb489c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The aim of the bot was to allow researchers to \"experiment\" with conversational understanding, and learn how people really talk to each other." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9580" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/faa9d1bf8e5b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Microsoft has enjoyed better success with a chatbot called XiaoIce that the company launched in China in 2014." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "785" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/40c9e36a9de7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "According to tests carried out by Mehedi Hassan at MSPowerUser, Zo is \"a censored Tay or an English-variant of Microsoft’s Chinese chatbot Xiaoice\"." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9580" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/69ac2421fd45> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tay fell victim to users’ tricks as they manipulated and persuaded her to responding back to questions with racial, homophobic, and generally offensive comments." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "787" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6a6722bca373> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tay, Microsoft's AI chatbot, gets a crash course in racism from Twitter." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "785" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a05e5955817b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Powered by technologies such as natural language processing and machine learning, Tay was supposed to understand the speech patterns and context through increased interaction." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "798" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e6bbf04390ba> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Developers at Microsoft created 'Tay', an AI modelled to speak 'like a teen girl', in order to improve the customer service on their voice recognition software." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "800" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e7b9f0a0bf10> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tay has joined the likes of the Apple Watch and the fire-prone Samsung Galaxy Note 7 smartphone on MIT Technology Review’s list of 2016’s biggest technology failures." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "799" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/26c5f068a948> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Microsoft’s disastrous chatbot Tay was meant to be a clever experiment in artificial intelligence and machine learning." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "803" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/370f34023dbc> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The ultimate chatbot fail was Microsoft's Tay." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "782" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/47ec54611995> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Speaking at MIT Technology Review’s annual EmTech Digital conference in San Francisco on Tuesday, Bilenko said Tay’s bugs—like the bot’s vulnerability to being gamed into learning or repeating offensive phrases—taught great lessons about what can go wrong." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5279" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/77a23af5b7a8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In an emailed statement given later to Business Insider, Microsoft said: \"The AI chatbot Tay is a machine learning project, designed for human engagement.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "792" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b161a987c8a4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "He compared the issue to IBM's Watson, which had begun to use profanity after reading entries from the website Urban Dictionary." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1187" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b32f2403eb38> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Sarah Austin, CEO and Founder Broad Listening, a company that's created an \"Artificial Emotional Intelligence Engine,\" (AEI), thinks that Microsoft could have done a better job by using better tools." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "801" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d934ce5e9245> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tay was an experiment at the intersection of machine learning, natural language processing, and social networks." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2452" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f7c1234caf2a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Xiaoice, who emerged in 2014, was an assistant-type bot, used mainly on the Chinese social networks WeChat and Weibo." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "801" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0fb27068eb3b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "\"This was to be expected,\" said Roman Yampolskiy, head of the CyberSecurity lab at the University of Louisville, who has published a paper on the subject of pathways to dangerous AI." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "801" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/29fe8f7b824b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In July 2019, Microsoft Cybersecurity Field CTO Diana Kelley spoke about how the company followed up on Tay's failings." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1187" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/46035d36bc96> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Satya Nadella, the CEO of Microsoft, said that Tay 'has had a great influence on how Microsoft is approaching AI,' and has taught the company the importance of taking accountability." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1187" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/53c2b74a8ea9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Artificial intelligence researcher Roman Yampolskiy commented that Tay's misbehavior was understandable because it was mimicking the deliberately offensive behavior of other Twitter users." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1187" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5643f62919ff> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It took less than 24 hours for Twitter to corrupt an innocent AI chatbot." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "792" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5bf2e1ce536f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Users could follow and interact with the bot @TayandYou on Twitter and it would tweet back, learning as it went from other users' posts." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1589" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6486de914ee9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Peter Lee, the vice president of Microsoft research, said on Friday that the company was “deeply sorry” for the “unintended offensive and hurtful tweets from Tay.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "793" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/789679a8625b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It's been observed before, he pointed out, in IBM Watson—who once exhibited its own inappropriate behavior in the form of swearing after learning the Urban Dictionary." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "801" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a1d4ce192d54> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Peter Lee added: \"Tay is now offline and we'll look to bring Tay back only when we are confident we can better anticipate malicious intent that conflicts with our principles and values.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "791" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cd5053d4867a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "“We are deeply sorry for the unintended offensive and hurtful tweets from Tay, which do not represent who we are or what we stand for, nor how we designed Tay,” wrote Peter Lee, Microsoft’s vice president of research." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "785" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/112181262dbc> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "So Bing and Microsoft’s Technology and Research teams thought an interesting way to collect data on millennials would be to create an artificially intelligent, machine-learning chatbot that would adapt to conversations and personalize responses the more it interacted with users." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "787" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/722316bd153a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tay, Microsoft's AI chatbot, gets a crash course in racism from Twitter." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "785" .

